Portrait of a fantasy D&D character. A ghoul (undead) that was once a cook. Grey desiccated skin, sunken eyes with a faint glow, fingers too long and bony. Crooked jaw, slightly open mouth. Wearing a stained cook's apron over tattered clothes. Holding a kitchen knife in one hand and a wooden spoon in the other. Expression: oddly friendly for an undead, almost welcoming. Background: ancient stone kitchen with copper pots, glass jars of colorful spices, and a cold hearth with faint embers. Style: realistic fantasy portrait with a touch of dark humor, warm dim lighting, waist-up.
